WEBVTT

00:00:00.730 --> 00:00:01.940
Azuma-kun.

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:03.560
I have nothing against you, but...

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.610
I can’t afford to lose either.

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:06.980
I’m going to win.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:13.240
With the pan au rustique created with these
Solar Hands and the Kaiyou yeast RAS.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:16.490
No way!

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:21.330
If you do that, the starch of the
dough will dissolve and it will break up.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:23.410
It’s all right like this.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.250
Like this...

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.790
Azuma Kazuma.

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:32.010
What in... What in the world are you doing?

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.330
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.250
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.580
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:43.990
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:49.220
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:53.060
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:10.140
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:18.110
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:25.940
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:33.700
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:41.170
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:50.550
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:59.310
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:03.570
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:06.520
is the light of only you.

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:10.310
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:15.120
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:22.840
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:27.330
Meister flying in the air!!

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:29.000
Who will be the winner?!

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:34.590
Stop messing around.

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:35.800
How long are you going to wash it?

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:36.880
Make bread properly.

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:39.050
Don’t be secretive about your bread!

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:40.890
Yeah. Are you listening?

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.430
M-Manager.

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.350
It’s turned into the situation we feared after all.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.690
I wonder if he’s all right. Azuma-san...

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.110
He’s probably fine.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:03:01.700
It’s not the first time that moron
has done something outrageous.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:02.780
You probably don’t need to worry.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:11.630
Umm... Are you an acquaintance of Azuma-san’s?

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:14.040
It’s me! Kawachi!

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:15.290
How can you not know that?!

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.710
I’ve just changed my hairstyle a little.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:19.630
Kawachi-san!

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:22.220
That’s not just a little. That hairstyle...

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.140
Yeah. An impressive afro.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.100
You’ve become a man,
haven’t you, Kawachi.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.890
M-Manager.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:38.740
I-It’s just as I thought.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:42.490
That church is a fearsome place
that lures everyone into an afro.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:44.870
It’s no such place!

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:49.370
Lately, this seems to be the only role I’m playing.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.750
What’s he doing?!

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:59.970
He’s left the washed dough
and started making a new dough.

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:02.090
What in the...?

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:04.470
In the end, the first dough
was a failure, huh?

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:07.720
Wasting food. Don’t do such things!

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:14.190
Honestly speaking, just breaking that
board wasn’t enough to satisfy me, but...

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.810
Oh?

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.780
What’s this board?

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:36.760
it appears that the filthy cockroach was an idiot who couldn’t do anything without his board.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.420
This is obvious, but...

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:46.760
if you wash the dough, the starch will disappear.

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:49.930
Only the sticky gluten component will remain.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:51.810
I guess I should conclude
that once his first attempt failed,

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:56.150
he had no choice but to start on a second attempt.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:57.810
But...

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:02.370
At this point in time, with a bread that you
make as an alternate plan along the way...

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:04.900
you really can’t win against me.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:07.820
How is it?

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:10.460
Look at my dough’s extensibility.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:13.800
This is the power of the Kaiyou yeast, RAS.

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:17.580
An abundance of moisture confers this
level of extensibility to the bread.

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:19.260
Azuma-kun.

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:22.720
I hoped to be able to have a
good match with you, but...

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:23.810
It’s a shame.

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:25.470
I’m just going to go ahead and win then.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:34.330
All that’s left is the baking.

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:36.770
All right!

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:39.020
Extend!

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:41.110
W-What the...?

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:43.480
W-What’s with that extensibility?

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:44.870
What the...?

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:48.420
His second dough extends like a mochi.

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:51.370
It’s much more extensible
than that Kanmuri guy’s dough.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:53.170
Impossible!

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:54.950
What’s with the dough’s extensibility?

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:56.420
Hey.

00:05:56.420 --> 00:06:02.010
Maybe he’s trying to make an even
more amazing bread than the <i>Japan</i> #44.

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:03.680
Yeah. Maybe.

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:04.960
It’s the finals after all.

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:20.930
Wh... What’s happening?

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:23.690
Kanmuri’s dough’s extensibility was astonishing enough.

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:27.820
However, Azuma’s dough is
definitely more extensible than Kanmuri’s.

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:33.530
If he’s increased the water content in some
way like Kanmuri has, I’d understand, but...

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:37.460
Can dough become all that extensible
after kneading it in the regular fashion?

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:43.710
When Azuma made his second dough, it didn’t look like there was any trick to it, but...

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:46.580
Even if you make a serious face... With that hairstyle...

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:48.340
There was a trick.

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:49.930
In the first dough...

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:51.800
The first dough?

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:54.930
I don’t know how he did it, but...

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:58.470
Azuma-kun’s dough turned out
more extensible than mine.

00:06:58.470 --> 00:07:03.810
A dough’s extensibility gives the
sticky quality that the Japanese really like.

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:07.360
If we were to predict an outcome from just that...

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:10.570
the possibility of me losing to him exists.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:12.570
But...

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:18.580
This pan au rustique has one more secret hidden within.

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:28.550
We will now begin the judging of the finals of the 39th Pantasia Newcomers’ Battle.

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:36.270
The judge of the finals is General Manager Kirisaki.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:44.360
You may present your bread
to General Manager Kirisaki.

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:48.070
The examiner is not Kuro-yan?

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:51.610
After he became the General Manager,

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:55.780
the judging of the finals became the
exclusive right of the General Manager.

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:56.660
Is that so...?

00:07:57.570 --> 00:07:59.790
The Afro Brothers...

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:06.080
General Manager Kirisaki.
I wonder what kind of reaction he’ll show.

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:07.760
I can’t even imagine it.

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:12.040
Both of you made dough with high extensibility.

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:13.260
But, looking at it after it’s baked...

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:16.260
Kanmuri has made a boulder shaped bread,

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:19.770
and Azuma-kun’s bread is balloon shaped.

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:23.770
This looks like it will be interesting.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.770
They look very different but...

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:30.280
The fact that they are both
amazing breads is very apparent.

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:34.280
Both of you have done very well so far.

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:39.110
Well then... I will begin with Kanmuri-kun’s bread.

00:08:39.110 --> 00:08:39.790
Okay.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:47.920
What a delicious looking pan au rustique.

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:52.750
I’m so going to become the General Manager.

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:53.800
And...

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.050
Someday... For sure.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:58.010
A boulder shaped bread.

00:08:58.010 --> 00:08:59.560
Pan au rustique.

00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:04.680
The bread with the highest water
content amongst French breads.

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:07.850
This is a sticky bread that the Japanese people like...

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:10.070
I wonder how it turned out with the Kaiyou yeast...

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:16.570
He... He ate it.

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:20.000
What... Exactly what kind of
reaction is he going to show us?!

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.240
He’s the General Manager.

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:26.000
There can be no doubt that he’ll
show some kind of extravagant reaction.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:31.750
Yes. This is wonderful.

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:35.890
Just as to be expected from Kuroyanagi’s junior.

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:40.920
Did... Did you see that Manager?

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:42.970
That’s just not right.

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:45.850
After all, he’s the General Manager.

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:48.730
Is that indifferent reaction really going to be forgiven?!

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:50.730
After all the trouble we’ve taken!

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:51.940
Calm down.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:53.440
But, Manager!!

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:55.990
Can’t you see it?

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:01.280
Raise your line of vision a little higher.

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:03.240
A little higher...?

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:08.040
Wh... What in the world is that?!

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:18.300
Wh... What in the world is that?!

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:21.180
That weird head!

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:22.810
P...P...P...

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:25.100
P...P...P... Peacock!

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:26.480
It’s peacock feathers!

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:28.020
It’s really gross!

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:30.520
I don’t think you can say that about other people.
It’s really gross!

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:34.150
Along with being an amazing baker,

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:36.320
like Dave, he has the power
to express the deliciousness

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:38.360
of something with his body in a tangible manner.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:40.700
He’s the Super Judge!

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.200
And by the way.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:46.250
Really bad, 0 to 19 points.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:47.830
A crow. Caw caw.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.420
Just bad, 20 to 39 points.

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:50.790
A sparrow. Chirp chirp.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:52.460
Regular, 40 to 59 points.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:54.210
A dove. Coo coo.

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:56.090
Just fine, 60 to 69 points.

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.470
A pheasant. Kyan kyan.

00:10:57.470 --> 00:10:59.300
Not too bad, 70 to 79 points.

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:00.140
A cuckoo.

00:11:00.140 --> 00:11:02.140
Delicious, 80 to 89 points.

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:03.850
A nightingale. Houkokogya.

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:05.530
Crazy delicious, 90 to 99 points.

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:06.140
A kingfisher.

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:07.350
Absolutely no complaints, 100 points.

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:07.720
A peacock.

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:09.310
This is how it is.

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:12.480
This is how it is, huh?

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:16.820
Man... It’s really annoying if you
have to match up the points to a bird.

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:17.610
Yeah.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:19.150
Anyway.

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:21.450
The results of this weird judgment style are...

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:24.710
It’s a fact that Kanmuri has
been awarded a perfect score.

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:27.160
Is Azuma all right?

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:30.580
If Kanmuri brought out the
peacock for a perfect score then,

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:32.790
even if Azuma ties,
we’ll just have a peacock.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:33.920
If we want to win,

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:37.710
then we have no choice but to bring out something like a phoenix with a big bang, right?

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:39.880
A phoenix...?

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:44.510
This pan au rustique...

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:45.890
Even in its home country, France,

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:50.140
it’s a difficult bread to make
for anyone but a first class baker.

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:55.150
And, I have never before eaten
a sample that was so delicious.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:59.290
This is not the power of just Kaiyou yeast, right?

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:00.950
Probably...

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:02.910
I believe that the flour you
used is different from regular flour.

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:04.200
Yes.

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:06.410
Impressive, General Manager Kirisaki.

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:11.170
In order to bring out the power of
the Taiensei reinforcing yeast RAS,

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:14.370
which I’ve personally developed, to it’s maximum...

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:17.130
I used a special flour.

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:20.480
Even from among the various soissons,
a French type of flour,

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:22.180
I chose one of superior quality.

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:26.140
When you say soissons, that’s the best
flour from among various types of flour.

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:29.060
If we’re talking about sake, it has to be Daiginjo.

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:31.020
If we’re talking about meat,
it has to be shimofuri sirloin.

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:33.600
If we’re talking about fish, it has to
be ootoro from natural black tuna.

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:36.150
If we’re talking about rice, it has
to be the brand name Koshihikari.

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:38.900
Man, I don’t quite get his examples.

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:42.780
Of course, this flour has been ground in a windmill.

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:46.910
This flour is responsible for
making the surface of the bread crisp,

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:50.870
while the soft an sticky
consistency of the insides is strengthened.

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:54.250
Huh... I guess there are many
different types of flour, huh?

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:59.960
Pan au rustique is French for
bread made with gum arabic.

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:02.470
In addition to the brand of the flour,

00:13:02.470 --> 00:13:05.550
if the flour has been milled in a windmill, the taste is completely different

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:07.220
from flour milled in a machine.

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:15.100
It’s really fragrant.

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:17.440
Azuma-kun.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:20.900
I may have yielded a few points to you when it comes to the extensibility of the flour...

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:25.200
But, this flour is my other secret weapon.

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:28.200
In addition to his new Kaiyou yeast,

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:30.830
he also had that flour hidden up his sleeve.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:33.580
Kanmuri Shigeru...

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:35.460
what kind of baker are you?!

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:37.960
Hello, everyone.

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:44.300
Oh my.

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:47.680
Why is it that everyone looks a little unwell?

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:49.510
All of you from the Southern Tokyo Branch, that is...

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:50.300
What do you want?

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:53.810
Oh, another part-timer, is it?

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:54.600
No!
Oh, another part-timer, is it?

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:55.270
Stop joking around!

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:57.310
Oh, scary!

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:59.820
But, I understand why you’d be irritated.

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:03.480
It’s because our Kanmuri has
tried a tad too hard, isn’t it?

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:05.860
Today, as an apology...

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:09.130
I got you some high grade kusaya.

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:10.490
This will become quite addictive, you know...

00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:12.010
Like we need something like that!

00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:14.010
Oh, please don’t be shy.

00:14:14.010 --> 00:14:15.010
Here you go.

00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:17.000
All right then. Take care.

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:22.250
That woman really annoys
the hell out of me.

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:23.840
Kawachi.

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:26.480
Just eat some kusaya and calm down.

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:27.650
You’re eating it?!

00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:28.880
It’s raw!

00:14:30.150 --> 00:14:31.020
It stinks.

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:32.070
Kawachi.

00:14:32.070 --> 00:14:34.700
Even if Kanmuri has gotten a perfect score,

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:37.100
we’ll win if Azuma scores higher than that.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:39.870
Higher than that, you say!

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:42.830
If we’re talking higher
than a perfect score...

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:44.360
there really must be
a phoenix coming, right?

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:46.250
Of course not!

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:47.360
No, huh?

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:49.570
Believe in him.

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:55.010
In Azuma... In his power.

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:57.700
Azuma’s... power.

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:03.170
Well then, I will now partake of Azuma’s bread.

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:12.940
Man... This looks like another delicious bread.

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:14.600
I’m so jealous.

00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:41.010
Peacock! It’s a peacock!

00:15:41.010 --> 00:15:42.350
It’s peacock feathers.

00:15:42.350 --> 00:15:44.430
We’re tied, Manager.

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:45.270
A tie?!

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:47.630
Kawachi, do you have empty
sockets where your eyes should be?!

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:50.010
Look at that!

00:15:58.530 --> 00:16:00.610
Look at that, Manager.

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:02.310
It’s like a phoenix.

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:04.810
Oh my.

00:16:24.010 --> 00:16:25.760
Wh... What is this?!

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:27.060
It wasn’t just a decoration!

00:16:27.060 --> 00:16:29.650
He had a real bird hidden inside.

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:35.020
Actually, his life has been a troubled one.

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:36.300
Is that so?

00:16:36.820 --> 00:16:39.810
But... if we don’t save Kawachi-san...

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:42.810
When he was a child...

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:46.660
he was abandoned in France by his father.

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:50.250
In order to earn a living, Kirisaki
began selling bread on the street.

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:52.170
But...

00:16:52.170 --> 00:16:53.830
however good the bread is...

00:16:53.830 --> 00:16:56.700
If it’s a child selling it on the
roadside, nobody will buy it.

00:16:57.170 --> 00:17:00.800
So, in order to attract
customers, he learned various tricks.

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:05.020
Even now, he’s able to produce
feathers from under his mask.

00:17:06.220 --> 00:17:06.970
But...

00:17:06.970 --> 00:17:09.710
To think that the peacock was actually still alive...

00:17:10.100 --> 00:17:11.710
Even I am in shock!

00:17:12.100 --> 00:17:13.650
It’s not the time to be in shock!

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:14.720
Do something!

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:29.450
So, does that mean that...
all the birds used in the grading system

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:32.410
are hidden away somewhere beneath that mask?

00:17:32.410 --> 00:17:33.420
I guess...

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:34.490
What kind of baker is he...?

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:37.990
T-To think that...

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:42.110
a crack would appear in this titanium alloy mask...

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:44.000
Moreover...

00:17:45.640 --> 00:17:49.000
My usually docile peacock, Coo, has run away!

00:17:49.930 --> 00:17:52.000
Azuma-kun’s fearsome bread!

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:53.560
What the...?

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:54.980
What’s happening?

00:17:54.980 --> 00:17:57.470
Since the peacock ran off, it may just be that...

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:00.230
I shall announce the results.

00:18:00.230 --> 00:18:01.220
Okay!

00:18:06.070 --> 00:18:07.940
Very well. I shall now announce it.

00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:12.480
The champion of the 39th
Pantasia Newcomers’ Battle is...

00:18:24.430 --> 00:18:25.850
Azuma Kazuma-kun.

00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:35.100
No way.

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:36.100
Amazing!

00:18:36.600 --> 00:18:37.270
He won!

00:18:37.270 --> 00:18:38.400
He won it!

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:39.590
He’s amazing!

00:18:40.690 --> 00:18:41.820
Please wait one moment!

00:18:41.820 --> 00:18:46.030
Azuma-kun’s bread may have been
better in terms of its sticky consistency.

00:18:46.030 --> 00:18:47.030
But!

00:18:47.030 --> 00:18:51.440
My bread’s surface has a crisp consistency due to the use of the soissons flour.

00:18:52.580 --> 00:18:55.330
When you look at it fair and square,

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:59.250
I can’t imagine how my bread
could be inferior to Azuma-kun’s!

00:18:59.250 --> 00:19:01.000
Ex... Exactly!

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:04.010
What’s the criteria you used
to come to this conclusion?

00:19:04.010 --> 00:19:07.080
Let me explain that reason to you.

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:09.890
Senpai...

00:19:09.890 --> 00:19:10.800
Wait! Please wait!

00:19:11.220 --> 00:19:15.670
In the first place, do you know why
you lost on the dough’s extensibility?

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:19.140
I don’t know.

00:19:19.140 --> 00:19:21.680
I couldn’t possibly know, could I?

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:24.890
Azuma-kun washed his first dough and messed that up.

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:28.520
Azuma-kun’s bread after doing something so absurd...

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:31.770
The reason he washed his dough!

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:32.480
Could it be...?

00:19:32.990 --> 00:19:34.520
It looks like you’ve figured it out.

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:35.700
Yeah.

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:38.830
The technique that Azuma used is...

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:41.530
Vital Gluten!

00:19:41.790 --> 00:19:43.790
Vital Gluten?

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:46.740
I’m sure that you would know...

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:51.750
If you wash the dough after
kneading and preparing the gluten...

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:55.250
the starch component is washed
away, leaving the gluten behind.

00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:58.140
This is called Vital Gluten.

00:19:58.140 --> 00:20:03.140
When Azuma washed the first
dough, he made home-made Vital Gluten.

00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:06.350
He added this to the second dough to make the bread.

00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:07.440
In other words...

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:11.280
One extra helping of Vital
Gluten was added to regular bread.

00:20:11.280 --> 00:20:13.900
This made a Double Gluten bread
with twice the amount of gluten.

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:19.280
It’s true that its appearance
is round and soft.

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:22.000
But, in addition to improving its extensibility,

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:25.050
twice the amount of gluten
also results in

00:20:25.050 --> 00:20:28.580
the crust on the surface having a crunchy consistency.

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:30.580
B-But...

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:31.710
But!

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:36.580
You don’t usually use Vital Gluten in regular bread.

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:40.890
It’s common sense to use it in bread when you add oats or use high temperatures...

00:20:41.680 --> 00:20:42.800
Common sense, huh?

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:46.470
Shigeru.

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:49.480
We graduated from Harvard.

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:53.440
We know the “common sense”
techniques of using Vital Gluten.

00:20:53.820 --> 00:20:54.980
You dumbass.

00:20:54.980 --> 00:20:55.730
Don’t run!

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:56.730
That hurts!
Don’t run!

00:20:57.280 --> 00:20:59.490
Rather than that, who the hell are you?

00:20:59.490 --> 00:21:01.440
I’ll make you remember.

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:07.000
In contrast, Azuma has probably
never heard the term “Vital Gluten.”

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:10.410
I lost... to such an opponent...

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:13.950
It’s because you were bound by
knowledge. And that common sense.

00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:18.920
Hey, let me go!

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:20.380
It’s Kawachi!

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:21.850
You can’t remember?

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:25.560
What’s with that gross hairstyle?

00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:27.470
You also think so, right?

00:21:28.310 --> 00:21:30.390
You certainly need knowledge.

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:32.020
But...

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:33.810
as bakers...

00:21:33.810 --> 00:21:34.980
As creators...

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:37.480
Those of us who have the dreams and the passion

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:40.480
to be able to overturn common sense are the strongest.

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:46.950
Why?

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:48.330
Why is it?!

00:21:48.330 --> 00:21:50.140
I really can’t acknowledge this.

00:21:50.140 --> 00:21:51.500
I won’t acknowledge this.

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:53.670
Wai... What are you doing?

00:21:53.670 --> 00:21:55.460
Let me go!

00:21:56.300 --> 00:21:57.460
Are you going to toss him?

00:21:57.460 --> 00:21:58.670
We want to join in!

00:21:59.050 --> 00:22:00.420
Let’s do it! Let’s do it!

00:22:05.140 --> 00:22:05.680
And up! And up!

00:22:05.680 --> 00:22:06.720
Stop!
And up! And up!

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:08.270
Stop it!
And up! And up!

00:22:08.270 --> 00:22:11.850
And up! And up!

00:22:11.850 --> 00:22:15.560
To have the dreams and passion
to overturn common sense...

00:22:15.560 --> 00:22:25.530
And up! And up!

00:22:25.530 --> 00:22:26.450
Stop!

00:22:26.450 --> 00:22:28.790
Stop it!

00:22:28.790 --> 00:22:31.840
And up! And up!

00:22:54.480 --> 00:22:56.240
On this chest, big and strong

00:22:56.240 --> 00:22:58.360
A look that glitters and doesn't lose.

00:22:58.360 --> 00:23:00.360
That's what I searched for, fumbling in the wind.

00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:01.660
The answer for now is...

00:23:01.660 --> 00:23:04.580
For now, I'll watch the situation and wait for a chance.
I got the patience to wait at a distance.

00:23:04.580 --> 00:23:06.370
A prisoner who just screams is no good.

00:23:06.370 --> 00:23:08.160
Just Follow Me! I'll lend you my shoulder occasionally.

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:18.260
It's by no means a fleeting dream.

00:23:18.260 --> 00:23:21.140
Let this sentiment reach you. Heart to Heart, Soul to Soul.

00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:23.180
The seasons turn. Splendid as a spring storm.

00:23:23.180 --> 00:23:24.590
Win Big is the motto.

00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:29.390
Does a thing like eternity really exist?

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:31.230
And so we... C'mon.

00:23:32.610 --> 00:23:36.780
Yeah, yeah, we live to touch the one shining moment.

00:23:53.710 --> 00:23:57.590
To all the soldiers fighting today using the tail wind...

00:24:05.460 --> 00:24:06.220
Kawachi!

00:24:06.220 --> 00:24:07.460
What is it?

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:09.010
You have the main role in the next episode!

00:24:09.010 --> 00:24:09.930
What?

00:24:09.930 --> 00:24:11.970
Just try doing something boring at Golden Time.

00:24:11.970 --> 00:24:13.890
It will be your responsibility entirely.

00:24:13.890 --> 00:24:14.930
What?!

00:24:14.930 --> 00:24:16.320
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.320 --> 00:24:17.140
What!!

00:24:17.140 --> 00:24:19.060
Kawachi. A man’s hard training!

00:24:19.060 --> 00:24:19.980
Be sure to watch.

00:24:20.350 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.150 --> 00:24:24.980
Gluten turns bread sticky.

00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:26.610
When you knead flour and water together,

00:24:26.610 --> 00:24:29.570
two different protein components, glutenin and gliadin, complex together to form gluten.

00:24:29.570 --> 00:24:31.740
So, be sure to knead your dough well!

00:24:31.740 --> 00:24:32.960
Oh!
